# Served by Cloudflare Workers Static Assets. Astro copies this file from
# public/ into dist/, where the assets runtime picks it up; it is never served
# as content itself.
#
# Each path pattern appears EXACTLY ONCE below. A pattern listed twice does not
# merge — the later block replaces the earlier one wholesale, which silently
# drops whatever the first block set. Group every header for a path together.

# Everything, including the 404. `not_found_handling: 404-page` serves the 404
# body at whatever URL was requested, so a rule on `/404.html` would never match
# a real miss; the baseline here is what actually covers it.
#
# 'unsafe-inline' for styles is required, not sloppiness: Astro's Fonts API
# emits its @font-face rules as an inline <style>, and the page's own CSS is
# inlined too (the whole document is a few kB, so a separate request would cost
# more than it saves). It buys an attacker nothing here — a fully static page
# with no user input and nothing reflected from the URL has no injection point
# for an inline style to arrive through.
#
# script-src 'self' exists for one file: the hashed /_astro bundle that decodes
# the obfuscated mailto. Keeping it out of an inline block is the whole reason
# that script lives in a module rather than in the markup.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# The FXCommands landing site is a separately built static bundle vendored in
# whole, and it needs a looser policy than the front page for two reasons:
#
#   - Its pages carry an inline <script type="module"> and an inline <style>,
#     so both directives need 'unsafe-inline'. Rebuilding someone else's output
#     to hoist two blocks out of the markup is not worth the churn.
#   - /fxcommands/migrate dynamically imports JSZip from cdn.jsdelivr.net to
#     rewrite Stream Deck profiles in the browser. That host must be in
#     script-src or the migrator silently fails to load and the page shows its
#     "check your ad blocker" error. It is the only external resource anything
#     on this origin fetches; every other off-site URL here is an anchor.
#
# The structural directives that actually matter (frame-ancestors, base-uri,
# object-src, form-action) are still locked down.
#
# The `!` line is load-bearing. Without it BOTH policies are emitted, and a
# browser given two CSP headers enforces each independently — the effective
# policy is their intersection, so the strict `script-src 'self'` above would
# still block the inline module and the JSZip import and the migrator would
# break. Removing the inherited header first is what makes this an override
# rather than an addition. Verified against `wrangler dev`: one CSP on every
# path, strict everywhere except here.
/fxcommands/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'

# Content-hashed by both builds, so a filename changes whenever its bytes do.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/fxcommands/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The HTML is the only thing that changes between deploys and it is a few kB.
# Revalidate every time rather than serve a stale page.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Proof-of-identity file. Short cache so a key rotation propagates promptly.
/.well-known/keybase.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/well-known/keybase.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
